      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ab3ad272b67505f726c2a8f|full_name}: Changing bindings in SteamVR should not be necessary at all to have the thumbsticks operate identically to Oculus Touch/Index controllers. The game doesn't even recognize they're WMR controllers at all; it treats them exactly like Vive wands, including the outline for interactions. Back when I was using WMR, there's no way I would've gone through the hassle of changing the bindings myself. It's more complicated than it should be (just looking at the menu is like \"omg what is even going on\") and was simply easier to just grab random ones off Steam workshop (since they're pretty much literally all named the same thing) until I got the right one.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
